<section class="blk blk--first">
  <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lead">The honest version is short: right now, this site collects nothing about you, because no form on it is live yet. This notice explains who is responsible, what will change when a sign-up does go live, and what we will never do.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">01 · What we collect today</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Today, nothing.</h2>
  <p>There is no live sign-up, pledge, or contact form on this site yet, so there is nothing for us to collect and nothing stored about your visit. The site sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and makes no third-party requests — every asset is served from uncost.org, which you can confirm in your browser’s network tab. That is why there is no cookie banner: there is nothing to consent to.</p>
  <p>When a sign-up form does go live, it will collect only what you type in (an email address, and anything else you choose to add), this notice will be updated to say so before that happens, and nothing here is retroactive.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">02 · Who is responsible</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Who holds your data.</h2>
  {#- SPONSOR-GATED · COUNSEL-GATED: the data controller below is PROVISIONAL. The
     controller identity changes once Uncost is incorporated and/or a fiscal
     sponsor is confirmed, and the wording must be confirmed with counsel before
     any form goes live. Update this line at the sponsor/counsel gate. -#}
  <p>Uncost is not yet incorporated. Until it is, the person responsible for any personal data this project handles is the founder operating the unincorporated project Uncost. This is provisional and will be confirmed with counsel, and updated here, once the legal home (incorporation or a fiscal sponsor) is settled.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">03 · Minimum age</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Who can sign up.</h2>
  {#- COUNSEL-GATED: the minimum-age threshold below is the intended DESIGN, not a
     finalised legal position. Confirm 18+ (and any guardian handling) with counsel
     before a sign-up form goes live. -#}
  <p>The design is that sign-ups are for adults: when a form goes live, signing up will ask you to confirm you are 18 or older. This is the intended rule and will be confirmed with counsel before any form opens.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">04 · What we never do</p>
  <h2 class="sec">What we never do.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We never sell, rent, or trade your personal data.</li>
    <li>We never use your details for partisan political targeting.</li>
    <li>We never require payment to take part.</li>
    <li>We never track you across other sites.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">05 · Reach us</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Questions about privacy.</h2>
  <p>If you have a question about privacy — now, or once sign-ups open — write to us at {{ mail.email() }} and a human will reply.</p>
</section>
